# EXPECT: observed module name 'f' is both a function definition and a top-level binding
#
# Round 61 found this direction of the observed kind-flip silently wrong:
# with the assigns BEFORE the define, the VM rebinds the name to the
# FUNCTION at the define's execution point, but compiled functions execute
# nothing at their statement position -- the env kept the stale number and
# the AOT printed 4 where the VM prints <fn f>, both rc 0. Round 61 added
# a direction check; round 62 measured three holes in the direction check
# itself and superseded it with a WHOLESALE refusal of the flip class
# (see refuse/observed_kind_flip.eigs for the full ledger). This fixture
# keeps the round-61 shape pinned under the round-62 message.
#
# Envelope shape: the VM RUNS this (rc 0, prints stab=0 then <fn f>).

f is 3.0
f is 4.0
print of ("stab=" + (str of (stable of f)))
define f() as:
    return 9
print of f
